+        \paragraph{Configuration-resolved spectroscopic-response guard.}
+        \label{par:canon_configuration_resolved_spectroscopic_response_guard}
+        \textbf{[CANON / RESPONSE-DEPENDENCY GUARD].}
+        A transition-frequency shift associated with an SST configuration $K$ is not
+        an additional mass formula.  It is defined by the variation of a transition
+        energy,
+        \begin{align}
+            \Delta E_i^{(K)}
+            &\equiv
+            E_{i,e}^{(K)}-E_{i,g}^{(K)},
+            &
+            \nu_i^{(K)}
+            &\equiv
+            \frac{\Delta E_i^{(K)}}{h},
+            \label{eq:canon_configuration_transition_energy_def}\\
+            \delta\nu_i^{(K)}
+            &=
+            \frac{1}{h}\,\delta\!\left(\Delta E_i^{(K)}\right)
+            =
+            \frac{1}{h}
+            \sum_A
+            \frac{\partial\Delta E_i^{(K)}}{\partial q_A^{(K)}}
+            \,\delta q_A^{(K)}
+            +O(\delta q^2),
+            \label{eq:canon_configuration_spectroscopic_linear_response}
+        \end{align}
+        where $q_A^{(K)}$ denotes a declared set of independent state variables.
+        Admissible examples include $M_K$, an inertia tensor $I_{K,ab}$, resolved
+        geometric or contact variables, and the clock factor.  Equation~\eqref{eq:canon_configuration_spectroscopic_linear_response}
+        defines only the dependency structure of a future response theory.  It does
+        not presently derive atomic levels, selection rules, or transition strengths.
+
+        \textbf{[CANON / NO-DOUBLE-COUNTING RULE].}
+        Because $\mathcal H(K)$ is already contained in the canonical kernel $\Xi_K$,
+        $\delta\mathcal H_K$ and $\delta\Xi_K$ must not be treated as independent
+        fit directions unless an explicit change of variables, projection, or
+        orthogonalization is supplied.  One may use either the compressed kernel
+        response $\delta\Xi_K$ or a resolved basis such as
+        $\{\delta C_K,\delta L_K,\delta\mathcal H_K,\delta k_K\}$, but not both
+        without an independently specified dependency matrix.
+
+        \textbf{[CANON / NON-PREDICTION GUARD].}
+        The present canon contains no first-principles SST derivation of a complete
+        atomic energy functional $E_{n\ell jm}^{(K)}$.  Consequently, generalized
+        isotope-shift or King-plot residuals may be used as research diagnostics, but
+        they do not by themselves identify an SST sector or constitute a prediction
+        of atomic spectroscopy.  The corresponding response programme is retained in
+        the research track.
+
